column3:
I have seen what {actor_name:7}{possessive_suffix}
power can do. It is
remarkable.{page_break}How could someone with
such gifts be held
against her will?{end_wait}

I won't give up on
{actor_name:7}. Not now.
She's our hope.{page_break}But hope isn't all.
We owe {actor_name:7}
more than prayers.{end_wait}

If {actor_name:7}
were here, I'd ask
what she thought.{page_break}But she's not.
We have to choose
what comes next.{end_wait}

Faran and his wife
raised {actor_name:7}
as their own.{page_break}The town calls her
its hope. To them,
{actor_name:7} is family.{end_wait}

Faran believes {actor_name:7}
is alive because of her
power.{page_break}I cannot rest until
I see her with my
own eyes.{end_wait}
